ce | $\\text{fl oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nTherefore, from the given options, the only unit of volume is \"gallon.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5fb4dd1c-93fb-5dc6-9046-9519ae49c22c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5fb4dd1c-93fb-5dc6-9046-9519ae49c22c" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fb4dd1c-93fb-5dc6-9046-9519ae49c22c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-052de27f-9024-580b-9a81-f42b8b029ab1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5b57c03-9174-52f9-bfd7-81cc5a3ea5b2" "answer-052de27f-9024-580b-9a81-f42b8b029ab1" "answer-e5a64a30-36b6-55d8-b908-7c23ebb1ba25" "answer-0a37a292-7ca5-5192-9524-17a833c43120" "answer-9556eb6b-421d-58eb-9066-c8fb90c20707"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5b57c03-9174-52f9-bfd7-81cc5a3ea5b2" :answer/id #uuid "f5b57c03-9174-52f9-bfd7-81cc5a3ea5b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "feet" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-052de27f-9024-580b-9a81-f42b8b029ab1" :answer/id #uuid "052de27f-9024-580b-9a81-f42b8b029ab1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "gallons" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5a64a30-36b6-55d8-b908-7c23ebb1ba25" :answer/id #uuid "e5a64a30-36b6-55d8-b908-7c23ebb1ba25" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "meters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a37a292-7ca5-5192-9524-17a833c43120" :answer/id #uuid "0a37a292-7ca5-5192-9524-17a833c43120" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "ounces" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9556eb6b-421d-58eb-9066-c8fb90c20707" :answer/id #uuid "9556eb6b-421d-58eb-9066-c8fb90c20707" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "square inches" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198669 :question/worked-solution "A table showing the customary units of volume is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Gallon | $\\text{gal}$ | $1\\,\\text{gal}=8\\,\\text{pints}$ |\n| Pint | $\\text{pt}$ | $1\\,\\text{pt}=2\\,\\text{cups}$ |\n| Cup | $-$ | $1\\,\\text{cup}=8\\,\\text{fl oz}$ |\n| Fluid ounce | $\\text{fl oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\text{gallon}$ is equivalent to $8\\,\\text{pints}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186194645 :answer-field/correct 17592186194646 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-36197295-ff24-5cc2-86bf-da1d0aa5bd10" :question/id #uuid "36197295-ff24-5cc2-86bf-da1d0aa5bd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-164395" :question/problem "A laboratory beaker has a volume of $1$ cup. What is this volume in fluid ounces?" :question/worked-solution "A table showing the customary units of volume is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Gallon | $\\text{gal}$ | $1\\,\\text{gal}=8\\,\\text{pints}$ |\n| Pint | $\\text{pt}$ | $1\\,\\text{pt}=2\\,\\text{cups}$ |\n| Cup | $-$ | $1\\,\\text{cup}=8\\,\\text{fl oz}$ |\n| Fluid ounce | $\\text{fl oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\text{cup}$ is equivalent to $8\\,\\text{fluid ounces}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-059c2f28-de07-5c7b-89b8-76b63496174d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-059c2f28-de07-5c7b-89b8-76b63496174d" :answer-field/id #uuid "059c2f28-de07-5c7b-89b8-76b63496174d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fe26694f-be4d-5dfb-b083-290974cd7d7b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c56f6327-55ba-5ce1-85a6-378cc7b98f52" "answer-666c3064-6bcb-5e18-86d0-49c6edeb78f3" "answer-c0c0840c-23cc-5523-b40a-51a8c6896ed1" "answer-552b638d-8d0a-56b5-b84b-ec230fed4d5c" "answer-fe26694f-be4d-5dfb-b083-290974cd7d7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c56f6327-55ba-5ce1-85a6-378cc7b98f52" :answer/id #uuid "c56f6327-55ba-5ce1-85a6-378cc7b98f52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25\\,\\text{fluid ounces}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-666c3064-6bcb-5e18-86d0-49c6edeb78f3" :answer/id #uuid "666c3064-6bcb-5e18-86d0-49c6edeb78f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5\\,\\text{fluid ounces}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0c0840c-23cc-5523-b40a-51a8c6896ed1" :answer/id #uuid "c0c0840c-23cc-5523-b40a-51a8c6896ed1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{fluid ounces}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-552b638d-8d0a-56b5-b84b-ec230fed4d5c" :answer/id #uuid "552b638d-8d0a-56b5-b84b-ec230fed4d5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{fluid ounces}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe26694f-be4d-5dfb-b083-290974cd7d7b" :answer/id #uuid "fe26694f-be4d-5dfb-b083-290974cd7d7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{fluid ounces}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199494 :tutorial/content "**Measuring** means finding a number that describes the size of something. The most popular measurement system within the scientific community is the **metric system**. \n\nWe determine how much space an object occupies by measuring its **volume**. We use **volume units** to specify an object's volume. \n\nA common metric unit of volume is the **liter,** which we denote using the symbol \"$\\textrm{L}$.\" We can use **measuring jugs** like the ones below to measure the volume of a liquid.\n\n![](images/fa/fa15e2d9b446412876732435aa06b8117fbb4903ab179e4cc64c50da4868fee7.png)\n\nWe use **milliliters** to measure smaller volumes. The symbol for milliliters is \"$\\textrm{mL}.$\" The prefix $\\textrm m$ stands for **milli,** which means $\\dfrac{1}{1\\,000}.$ Therefore, $1\\,\\textrm{mL}$ equals $\\dfrac{1}{1\\,000}\\,\\textrm L.$\n\nNotice that if we add $1\\,\\textrm{mL}$ to itself $1\\,000$ times, we get exactly $1\\,\\textrm{L}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{1\\,000\\text{ times}}{\\overset{⏞}{1\\,\\text{mL}+1\\,\\text{mL}+⋯+1\\,\\text{mL}}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{1\\,000}\\,\\text{L}+\\frac{1}{1\\,000}\\,\\text{L}+⋯+\\frac{1}{1\\,000}\\,\\text{L} & = \\\\ 1\\,000\\times \\frac{1}{1\\,000}\\,\\text{L} & = \\\\ \\frac{1\\,000\\times 1}{1\\,000}\\,\\text{L} & = \\\\ \\frac{1\\,000}{1\\,000}\\,\\text{L} & = \\\\ 1\\,\\text{L}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{mL}$ equals $1\\,\\textrm{L},$ as stated in the diagram." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199505 :tutorial/content "Another way to measure volume is to use **customary units.** The most common customary units for volume are **fluid ounce**, **cup**, **pint**, and **gallon**.\n\nA table showing the customary units of volume is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Gallon | $\\textrm{gal}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{gal} = 8\\,\\textrm{pints}$ |\n| Pint | $\\textrm{pt}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{pt} = 2\\,\\textrm{cups}$ |\n| Cup | $-$ | $1\\,\\textrm{cup} = 8\\,\\textrm{fl oz}$ |\n| Fluid ounce | $\\textrm{fl oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nNote that \"gallons\" is the largest volume unit, and \"fluid ounces\" is the smallest. \n\nCustomary units are not standard in the scientific community. However, they are commonly used in the United States and other countries." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198503 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
